{"rules":{"levels":"C, B and A conversations usually open at support levels 2, 3 and 4. Not every pair has all three — some have only C, or only B and A.","howToRaise":["Give gifts to Guests in Dagsion.","Share meals at the inn with three characters, up to three meals per week. A Guest must have received a gift once before joining a meal.","Watch theatre performances with the protagonist and a Guest.","Once recruited, fight adjacent to allies and use Link Attacks.","Weekly activities reset on Sunday.","Replaying a chapter keeps support gains."],"caveats":["View conversations at the taverns in Dagsion, near the colosseum or in Lowtown. A padlock indicates an unmet requirement.","Some conversations require recruitment, route progress, another conversation, or a particular availability window. There is no verified universal recruitment rule for every pair.","A numeric support level can rise even for a pair without listed conversations. An unlisted pair here means no confirmed matrix entry, not a limit on support growth.","Which ranks exist comes from Fire Emblem Wiki’s full support lists, cross-checked with a community requirements spreadsheet. Dashed ranks are listed by only one inconsistent source.","Most “conditions not met” padlocks clear once both characters are recruited, unless another requirement is shown.","Scenes you mark as watched are shared by all your save files — marking one in any playthrough marks it everywhere.","“Ready to view” means your support level and your journey in More both allow it, and both characters can be in your army on this path. Inn opening times, chapter windows and the conditions shown on each conversation still apply in the game.","Inns open for supports from Chapter 4 of each Part I path, and in Part II during Chapters 1–4. Nothing can be viewed in the Prologue.","Some A conversations must be viewed before Part III begins; they are marked “Before Part III”. Others first open in Part II or Part III.","Every pair starts at support l